course: dictionary
lesson: 13529
title: Impersonation: copying or pretending
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: An impersonation is when someone copies another person, or pretends to be them. It is a noun, so you can say an impersonation or some impersonations. «Sam did a brilliant impersonation of our head teacher.» Sam copies the way the head teacher talks and moves, so the class laughs. That is the funny kind.
explain: The other meaning is serious. «The email was an impersonation of the bank, and it asked for our passwords.» The email pretends to be the bank to trick people. Clues like asked for our passwords tell you this is the bad kind, and it can be a crime.
explain: Ask yourself: is the person having fun, or trying to fool someone for money or secrets? The words around the word give you the clue. Do an impersonation of usually means the funny kind, so read the rest of the sentence carefully.
fact: An impersonation is a funny copy of someone's voice, way of speaking or actions.
fact: Impersonation can also mean pretending to be someone else to trick people, and this can be a crime.
fact: Impersonation can be countable (an impersonation, impersonations) or uncountable (impersonation in general).
fact: Scammers use impersonation of banks, companies or officials to get money or passwords from people.
fact: Useful phrases: do an impersonation of, a brilliant impersonation, identity impersonation.
exercise: «Mia did a brilliant impersonation of her grumpy cat.» What is an impersonation here? | *A funny copy of how someone moves and talks | A serious crime | A loud shout | A new pet
exercise: «The message pretended to be from the bank and asked for passwords.» What is this an example of? | A school trip | A type of dance | A kind of weather | *Impersonation used to trick people
exercise: «The comedian's ___ of the prime minister had the whole audience laughing.» Which word fits the gap? | puzzle | *impersonation | receipt | tunnel
test: Which sentence uses impersonation in the serious sense? | Dad's impersonation of a robot made us giggle. | The comedian's impersonation of a famous singer was brilliant. | *A caller claimed to be from the bank to get Tom's card number. | Lily did a great impersonation of her teacher at the party.
test: What should you do if you get a message pretending to be from your bank? | Reply with your password so they can check it | *Do not click the links, and tell a trusted adult or the bank | Forward it to all your friends | Send money to fix the problem
exam: In «The scammer's impersonation of the police fooled Grandma», what does impersonation mean? | A funny copy of a voice | *Pretending to be someone else to trick people | A kind of food | A famous poem
